1. You are way too excited to get started-- The 1046 Error.
MySQL is a little Matryoshka doll of a program. If you're missing the first doll, how can you expect to access the others? That's how I rationalize the 1046 error. Sometimes you just get way too excited about your assignment, or it's been a minute since you've looked at it, and the simplest things turn into your biggest hurdles. 
![A screenshot highlighting the MySQL 1046 error. The error itself reads: "ERROR 1046 (AD000): No database selected"](https://github.com/images/Hendricks_screenshot_gCloud_MySQL1046.png)

Thankfully it's an easy enough fix, just select your database with "use [database name]". 
![A screenshot showing the the successful change in database and proof by inserting items into a table within that database.](https://github.com/images/Hendricks_screenshot_gCloud_MySQL1046fix.png)

